Time Complexity:
O(n)

Space Complexity:
O(1)

Approach:
1. Initialize winner as the first element and winCount = 0
2. Traverse the array from index 1
3. Compare current winner with the current element
4. If current element is larger, make it the new winner and set winCount = 1
5. Otherwise, increment winCount
6. If winCount becomes greater than or equal to k, return the winner
7. If no element achieves k consecutive wins, return the maximum element stored in winner




class Solution {
    public int getWinner(int[] arr, int k) {
        int winCount = 0;
        int winner = arr[0];
        for(int i=1; i<arr.length; i++){
            if(winner < arr[i]) {
                winner = arr[i];
                winCount = 1;
            }
            else {
                winCount++;
            }

            if(winCount >= k) return winner;
        }
        return winner;
    }
}
